= BITwiki V2 =

BITwiki V2 is a refactor of the public BITwiki knowledge architecture. The live wiki remains the reference for existing content while V2 rebuilds how that content is organized, related, reused, and queried.

== Purpose ==
BITwiki turns useful knowledge into durable, structured, modular, source-grounded memory that humans and machines can retrieve, compose, verify, and reuse.

== Core model ==
A knowledge page has four independent concerns:

* '''Identity''' — namespace, entity type, domain, and relationships.
* '''Content''' — reusable semantic sections called [[BITwiki:Book matter|Book Matter]].
* '''Epistemics''' — sources, evidence, provenance, status, confidence, uncertainty, and verification.
* '''Presentation''' — templates, modules, portals, and generated navigation.

These concerns must not be collapsed into one category tree.

== Native MediaWiki first ==
* Namespaces separate system roles and page classes.
* Categories group pages for human classification and navigation.
* Semantic properties describe attributes and relationships.
* Templates provide consistent rendering and data entry.
* Modules contain reusable logic when templates are insufficient.
* Concepts are query-defined semantic collections, not a substitute namespace for ordinary concept articles.

